  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 340 AM MST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nThe rest of the week looks mostly uneventful after we finally say \nfarewell to this system by Wednesday. Ridging will try to build back \ninto the area, but the warming potential will be hampered by a few \nmoisture-starved closed lows moving across the western CONUS. As a \nresult, look for highs to remain generally close to seasonal \naverages from midweek through the weekend. The first closed low \naround Wednesday will bring a chance for a few rain / high elevation \nsnow showers, but most ensemble members send the tiny, compact \nsystem and the narrow band of precipitation potential to our south. \nThe next system looks to pass to our north over the weekend. The \nchance for precipitation is low with this one, but it may bring a \nsurge in gusty winds across the area Saturday and Sunday. Behind \nthis system, we should see cleaner ridging take over across the\nwestern CONUS. After a slightly cooler day Saturday, look for \ntemperatures to trend above seasonal averages Sunday and Monday.",
